  "notes": "Two branches of the same function, `fetchBestBuild` (PaperDownloader.swift:201-272), which is what both the Components-tab picker and `downloadLatestPaper`/`fetchLatestMetadata` (the create-flow \"download latest Paper\" path) actually call. Non-experimental: only STABLE-channel entries qualify; among them the highest numeric `id` wins regardless of how many BETA/ALPHA entries also exist (132 beats 131/130 beats the beta/alpha ones entirely -- they're never even compared once a STABLE entry qualifies). Experimental: only BETA/ALPHA entries qualify, and the function additionally refuses to return anything at all if the version has ANY STABLE build (`hasStableBuild`, lines 232, 267-269) -- true experimental (26.x-style) versions have never shipped a STABLE build, so this guard exists to stop a released 1.21.11-style version from ever appearing on the experimental track just because it once had a beta build during development. Build-id comparison is a plain highest-wins scan, same as the stable branch."
